        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SIM02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Sims</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>chemist</occupation>
                    <occupation>druggist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Sims is a chemist based in Norwich, from 1795 in partnership with <persName key="PIT02">John Pitchford</persName>, who
  can be identified through the circles of Norwich radicalism in which he appears. (See Jewson on Norwich and the French Revolution.)
  The two instances of 'Sims' and one of 'Sim's' in 1796 have been identified as this Sims.
  There is a 'Sims' in 1809 but this is in London rather than Norwich thus we cannot make the same identification. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> C.B. Jewson,<title>The Jacobin City: A Portrait of Norwich in its Reaction to the French Revolution 1788-1802</title>,  (Glasgow: Blackie, 1975).</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
